messages:
Maria: quick Q — our /v1/annotate endpoint is returning inconsistent shapes across codepaths: sometimes `metadata` is null, sometimes it's omitted. Clients are failing when they expect the key. Do we have a contract for "always key present vs key optional"?

Jonah: we never finalized that. there was an earlier note in the API doc but no enforced rule. cc @Kavi for runtime implications. https://github.com/redwood-inference/redwood/pull/1234 :eyes:

Kavi: my immediate thought: JSON Schema should accept both (type: ["object","null"]) but server behavior should be consistent. emitting absent vs null is a serialization choice. always-emitting keys simplifies typed clients; omitting saves bytes.

Maria: example payloads we see: 
```json
// happy path
{
  "id": "abc",
  "annotations": [{"label":"person","bbox":[1,2,3,4]}],
  "metadata": {"source":"camera-1"}
}

// edge path - explicitly null
{
  "id": "def",
  "annotations": [],
  "metadata": null
}

// legacy path - key missing entirely
{
  "id": "ghi",
  "annotations": [/*...*/]
  // no metadata key
}
```

Priya: for SDKs and downstream p99s we should pick a deterministic rule. my vote: always include `metadata` key and set it to null when there's no data. avoids a bunch of optional chaining everywhere. downside: slightly bigger payloads.

Kavi: I'm leaning same. operational caveat: streaming NDJSON endpoints (tooling & live tails) would need to emit a field per-line; cost increase is minimal. implementation: change serializer to emit keys when default value is null. also update our JSON Schema to explicitly list `metadata` as nullable rather than optional. example schema snippet: 
```json
"metadata": { "anyOf": [{"type":"object"}, {"type":"null"}], "description":"optional metadata, emitted as null when absent" }
```

Jonah: SDKs: I'll update TS types to `metadata: Record<string, any> | null` and add a compatibility layer that tolerates missing key for one release. will add unit tests asserting server either emits null or the key exists; compat test will accept missing for older canaries.

Maria: rollout proposal: behind a feature flag (canary) that flips serializer to always emit keys. default remains old behavior for now. if canary metrics look good we flip globally. Priya can coordinate region/tenant canary.

Kavi: I'll open the schema + server PR today and add a migration note. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/redwood/pull/1280 :shipit:

Jonah: I'll follow up with SDK PR and add a changelog entry. also adding an integration test that loads both old-style and new-style responses to ensure clients don't crash.

deploy-bot: canary deployed to eu-west-1 for tenant:acme at 1762501500 :rocket:

Maria: awesome — thanks everyone. action items: Kavi (schema + runtime PR), Jonah (SDK + tests), Priya (canary coordination). we'll check back once metrics from the canary are in. :thumbsup:
